    "$comment": "Percentiles from the top of each scenario's KovaaK's leaderboard, one array per window, easiest rank first. Read as one list across every window they are strictly decreasing, and that is the property that matters: the sweep that grades the population gives a player the same percentile on every board, so these values are the rank boundaries themselves and rank r holds the band between its own value and the next. A value that does not fall below the one before it is a rank superseded the moment it is reached, which is how ranks 4, 8 and 12 came to be held by nobody. npm run distribution is what checks it.",
